    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1081">

                <pb facs="0794" n="678" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg678"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/3866.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé O’Shaughnessy to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 27, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Garden effected transit of over 40 Americans from Mexico to Vera Cruz. The
                    British cruiser <hi rendition="#italic">Hermione</hi> took 1241 American
                    refugees from Tampico to-day. Americans arriving from Mexico City state that
                    Carden has done utmost for our nationals. I have great fear that several
                    Americans have been injured if not killed in Mexico City.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson O’Shaughnessy</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
